<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernat III of Besalú</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1111</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernat III was the last count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/besalu">Besalú</a>, in north-eastern Catalonia. He married Ximena, a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramon-berenguer-iii-of-barcelona">Ramon Berenguer III of Barcelona</a>, and when he died without children in 1111 the county passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> under an agreement with his father-in-law. Its absorption was a further step in the gathering of the Catalan counties by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-barcelona">House of Barcelona</a>.</p></div>
